        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Cognitive Dissonance: Performing Menial Tasks</title>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"MathJax-script\" async\n  src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\">\n</script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;\n    background: #1b3a5c;\n    color: #fff;\n  }\n  .page {\n    display: flex;\n    width: 1056px;\n    min-height: 816px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a6fa3 0%, #1b3a5c 60%);\n  }\n  /* Left panel */\n  .left {\n    width: 380px;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n    padding: 40px 38px 30px 38px;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .left .presents {\n    font-size: 17px;\n    line-height: 1.4;\n    color: #e8f2f8;\n    margin-bottom: 18px;\n  }\n  .left h1 {\n    font-size: 44px;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    margin: 0 0 20px 0;\n    color: #ffffff;\n  }\n  .left .study {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    color: #7fd4f5;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    margin-bottom: 40px;\n  }\n  .heads {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 22px;\n    margin-bottom: 45px;\n  }\n  .head-icon {\n    width: 90px;\n    height: 90px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.15);\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .head-icon svg { width: 46px; height: 46px; fill: #ffffff; }\n  .hr-line {\n    border: none;\n    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);\n    margin: 0 0 12px 0;\n  }\n  .refs {\n    font-size: 10px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: #cfe6f2;\n  }\n  .refs .label {\n    font-weight: 700;\n    letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n    display: block;\n  }\n\n  /* Right grid */\n  .right {\n    flex: 1;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n    grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 1fr);\n    gap: 2px;\n  }\n  .cell {\n    padding: 26px 28px;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .cell.light { background: #1f5f8b; }\n  .cell.dark { background: #142d47; }\n  .cell h2 {\n    font-size: 19px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    color: #ffffff;\n  }\n  .cell p {\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    margin: 0;\n    max-width: 62%;\n    color: #eaf2f7;\n  }\n  .icon-slot {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 26px;\n    top: 26px;\n    width: 70px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 10px;\n  }\n  .icon-slot svg { width: 48px; height: 48px; fill: #58c4ec; }\n  .icon-slot.white svg { fill: #ffffff; }\n  .placeholder-note {\n    font-size: 9px;\n    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5);\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n  <div class=\"left\">\n    <div class=\"presents\">The National Centre<br>for Neurology and Brain<br>Mechanics Presents</div>\n    <h1>Cognitive Dissonance: Performing Menial Tasks</h1>\n    <div class=\"study\">Study conducted by Jonas Festinger,<br>Marcus Carlsmith &amp; Gabriel Chessman</div>\n\n    <div class=\"heads\">\n      <div class=\"head-icon\" title=\"[Icon: head with gear]\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 2a10 10 0 1 0 10 10A10 10 0 0 0 12 2zm3 11.5a1.5 1.5 0 1 1 1.5-1.5 1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5zm-6 0A1.5 1.5 0 1 1 10.5 12 1.5 1.5 0 0 1 9 13.5z\"/></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"head-icon\" title=\"[Icon: head with exclamation mark]\">\n        <span style=\"font-size:40px; font-weight:700;\">!</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"head-icon\" title=\"[Icon: head with question mark]\">\n        <span style=\"font-size:40px; font-weight:700;\">?</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"hr-line\">\n    <div class=\"refs\">\n      <span class=\"label\">REFERENCES:</span>\n      Walsh, Karen., Kemputo, Odelle., \"The psychology of self-deception\"<br>\n      The Anaptic Journal, 2017 • Satuda, Evelyn., Temitope, Anya., \"Neuroscience<br>\n      of Decision-Making\" The Science Review, 2018 • Brahms, Hansen., Leigh,<br>\n      Anderson., \"The Need and Neurology for Happiness\", The Arch Journal, 2020\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"right\">\n\n    <div class=\"cell light\">\n      <h2>Purpose:</h2>\n      <p>Festinger, Carlsmith and Chessman wanted to understand if making people perform a menial task would result in cognitive dissonance as a result of forced compliance behavior.</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot\" title=\"[Icon: gear cluster and group of people]\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 2a10 10 0 1 0 10 10A10 10 0 0 0 12 2z\" opacity=\"0\"/></svg>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: gears]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: people group]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"cell dark\">\n      <h2>Hypothesis:</h2>\n      <p>When asked to do an unenjoyable task, people will not readily admit as much, and tell themselves and others it is actually enjoyable.</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot white\" title=\"[Icon: thumbs up and scale]\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: thumbs up]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: scale]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"cell light\">\n      <h2>Participants:</h2>\n      <p>In a lab setting, 71 male students as participants to perform a series of menial tasks (like turning pegs in a peg board for an hour).</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot\" title=\"[Icon: clock and circuit-like path]\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: clock]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: connector path]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"cell dark\">\n      <h2>Method:</h2>\n      <p>The participants were then paid either $1 or $20 to tell a waiting participant (a test confederate) that the tasks were really engaging and fun. Almost all of the participants agreed to walk into the waiting room and persuade the confederate that the boring experiment would be interesting.</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot white\" title=\"[Icon: speech bubble and hand with coin]\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: speech bubble]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: hand with coin]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"cell light\">\n      <h2>Results:</h2>\n      <p>When the participants were asked to evaluate the experiment, the participants who were paid only $1 rated the tedious task as more fun and enjoyable than the participants who were paid $20 to lie.</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot\" title=\"[Icon: upward arrow and star with plus]\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: arrow up]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: star with plus]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"cell dark\">\n      <h2>Conclusion:</h2>\n      <p>Getting paid $1 is not sufficient for lying, so those who were paid $1 experienced dissonance. These participants could only overcome that dissonance by coming to believe that the tasks really were interesting and enjoyable.<br><br>Being paid $20 provides a reason, therefore there is no dissonance.</p>\n      <div class=\"icon-slot white\" title=\"[Icon: hand pouring coin and head with gear]\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: hand/coin]</div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder-note\">[Icon: head with gear]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
